<title>USA: U.S. March non-farm payrolls rose 175,000.</title>
<headline>U.S. March non-farm payrolls rose 175,000.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Labor Department seasonally adjusted jobs data.</p>
<p> In 1,000s--Change     March   Feb--(Prev)   Jan-(Prev)  Mar96</p>
<p>  in Nonfarm Payrolls   175    293    339    259   247     171</p>
<p> Jobless Rate (Pct)     5.2    5.3    5.3    5.4   5.4     5.5</p>
<p>Earnings, Hours of Private, Non-Farm Production workers:</p>
<p>    -		     March    Feb-(Prev)    Jan-(Prev)  Mar96</p>
<p>Earnings/Hour(dollars)  12.15  12.10  12.09  12.05  12.06  11.68  Avg Weekly Hours	34.8   34.9   35.0   34.2   34.2   34.5</p>
<p> Manufacturing Hours   42.1   41.9   41.9   41.7   41.7   41.3</p>
<p> -Overtime Hours	  4.9    4.7    4.7    4.7    4.6    4.3</p>
<p>Non-Farm Month-On-Month Payroll Changes by Industry:</p>
<p>    In 1,000s --	 March   Feb--(Prev)   Jan-(Prev)</p>
<p> Goods-Producing	  -12    114    109     43    33</p>
